    {
      "id": "whats-open-how",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "What is actually open",
      "position": {
        "x": -440.6696141271455,
        "y": 403.6177964056794
      },
      "width": 623.6423537428395,
      "height": 500.7170106578932,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# What is actually open\n\nAfter the audits of 25 October, **updated 29 October**. Everything else is finished, archived, folded into one of these, or an idea. On the 25th, **28 task graphs were open**: five being worked, six that needed a quick check to close, and seventeen waiting. They are written here in the order I would take them, and each says what the next step is.\n\n**Since the 25th.** The Properties panel and the authoring contract are built and enforced: all 79 switches are a graph in canon, checked by a test, and edge animation and effects, node text styles and the dropdowns work. The library has a new root, a contracts index and a way back from every shelf. Every primitive page is on the new poster and has been checked against the code, and the Page Template is at the new port standard. A saved graph needs a root, and analytics is gone. Since the 28th: the Fragment primitive is a canon page with a working example (a fragment is a piece of a node, and the stand-in has an Expand button), a piece brings content and structure only unless the host grants its code and Bridges, a playing video or sound belongs to the node and survives a change of view, and publishing and deploying work again. Those streams are marked below; the rest of the page is as it was on the 25th.\n\nThe lists are in `plans/where-i-am`, which is generated from the graphs and can be run again. This page is by hand."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "whats-open"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792980551498,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "whats-open-one",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "1. In motion now",
      "position": {
        "x": -442.22126769801565,
        "y": 997.0910284731603
      },
      "width": 633.209440138814,
      "height": 760,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 1. In motion now (6)\n\nThese are the streams with work behind them. Take them first, since each is already loaded.\n\n1. **The library made current** (yours, `tasks/library-made-current`). New since the 25th. 21 done, 17 to do, 2 in progress, 2 waiting. Next: take Expand out of the Portal and onto the Import end of a Bridge, then rebuild the contracts that only had their structure converted, then the custom roots hearing and events across a Bridge. Waiting on you: what readers say about the wording of the primitive pages.\n2. **The Properties panel and the authoring contract** (yours, `tasks/properties-and-authoring-contract`). Mostly closed: twenty-eight done. Left: retire the old tables and keys, split `PropertiesPanel.js`, the Graph boundary review, the blank view on zoom, and a tutorial pass on zoom and edges. Waiting on you: the Starter's \"The Library\" route, which is yours to veto.\n3. **Canon templates in order** (yours, `tasks/canon-templates-in-order`). Five done, seven to do: the plan, thinking, handle and public arrival templates, then publish. The Page Template is now at the new standard (a Content node's ports on all five of its nodes). The Declaration Template waits on the custom roots hearing.\n4. **Primitives, self-documenting** (yours, `tasks/primitives-self-documenting`). The fifteen pages are staged and checked against the code, and the Script primitive has left the collection. Next: tutorial copy, one primitive at a time, then a cold read by someone who is not you. Waiting on you: the Environment, Ground and Event wording.\n5. **Twilite Zone graphs follow the view-shape rule** (yours, `tasks/canon-view-shape-consistency`). One blocked task, three to do. Next: unblock it.\n6. **Method calls leave a trace** (yours, `tasks/method-traceability`). Small, and it can wait. Next: only if a Method failure has had to be traced by hand."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "whats-open"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792980567294,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "whats-open-two",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "2. Check and close",
      "position": {
        "x": -440.17806757850377,
        "y": 1837
      },
      "width": 646.9171573058929,
      "height": 435.3450392873893,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 2. Check and close (6)\n\nEach says \"in progress\" and is mostly built. One short check in the app per graph, then close it or write down what is really left. These are the cheapest way to shrink the list, and they may turn up real bugs.\n\n- **Ports and handles interface** (yours). Core done; the rest moved to the Properties task. Check: does a Port configure from its panel?\n- **Workspace graph-node projection** (canon). The border handles and drops of this week. Check: drop a handle onto blank space, onto a graph, and onto another handle; the last is the one still open (endpoint drops as relationship operations).\n- **Workspace graph-space unification** (yours). Drag and hit testing work. Close it, noting that a browser proof is not possible without a test runner.\n- **Edge endpoint reassignment** (yours). `reconnectEdge` exists. Check: grab an edge end and move it; note what is missing (the smoke graph, the editor's selectors).\n- **Property node inline editor** (yours). The class and tests exist. Check: edit a Property in place, apply and cancel.\n- **Graph organization law** (canon). One task left, which is the templates stream. Close it, pointing there."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "whats-open"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792980584784,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "whats-open-three",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "3. Toward the beta",
      "position": {
        "x": 391.6385679308017,
        "y": 398.6600093140029
      },
      "width": 573.9894394749922,
      "height": 528.2417321456488,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 3. Toward the beta (9)\n\nThe product-facing list. They only make sense in relation to each other, so decide the order together.\n\n1. **Beta readiness** (canon). The umbrella: six done, five in progress, two to do. Read it first.\n2. **New user experience** (canon). One task, one question: how much the first screen should explain.\n3. **App settings panel and mouse sensitivity** (canon). A clear, bounded job with no panel yet. Good first build.\n4. **Diagnostics** (canon, May). An account diagnostics route exists; the durable, attributable surface does not.\n5. **Users** (canon, May). The account API and repo mappings exist. Rewrite the goal to say what is left before building anything.\n6. **Mouse controls: context menus** (canon). The radial menu is built. Check how complete the context menus are, then decide what is left.\n7. **Tutorial and how-to cluster** (canon). Beside the primitives' tutorial copy; do them together.\n8. **Declaration surfaces** (canon). From 24 September. Rewrite it in today's words (root, not Declaration) or fold it into the Properties task.\n9. **Workspace save and connection validation** (yours). Two draft tasks from 18 October. Keep, or fold into the workspace stream in part 2."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "whats-open"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792980639822,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "whats-open-four",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "4. Later",
      "position": {
        "x": 375.5001641505958,
        "y": 1006.848639725129
      },
      "width": 616.1206113637236,
      "height": 415.68062521644885,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 4. Later (5)\n\nReal, and not in anyone's way.\n\n- **Graph-scoped skills** (yours). Nothing in the code reads a `SKILL.md` from a graph. Nine tasks, three questions. A good idea with no urgency.\n- **Workspace topological adjacency** (yours). Goal \"proposed\", one decision pending: **your decision is needed before anything is built**. Apertures and bridge placement already exist.\n- **Question-driven explanation template** (yours). A prototype of seven classes and three specimens, for the templates stream when it has room.\n- **Bridge editor sections** (yours). Its first task is obsolete; the subject is real. Grants still sit in the Properties panel, so \"move them out\" is not done. Do it with the Properties work.\n- **Template video and UI polish** (yours). A demo-video task with eight untitled tasks. Yours to decide."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "whats-open"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792980617493,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "whats-open-five",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "5. Not today",
      "position": {
        "x": 354.08718498096306,
        "y": 1474.9424935085399
      },
      "width": 669.8849878788654,
      "height": 292.7958318903411,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 5. Not today (3)\n\nLeft alone on purpose.\n\n- **Intent-first authoring** (canon). Too vague to act on.\n- **Local node runtime** (canon). A different architecture from today's client-side editor. Decide whether it is still a direction.\n- **Bounded interactive markdown** (canon). A decision open since May."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "whats-open"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792980657338,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
